<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Friedberg (Hesse)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Friedberg is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wetterau">Wetterau</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> beside an imperial castle on a ridge. The town, an imperial city by 1211, and the castle community of the Burgraviate of Friedberg, governed by knights, were rival neighbours for centuries. Both passed to Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> in the early 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/friedberg-hesse.jpg" alt="Friedberg (Hesse)" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedberg_(Hessen)_Stadtkirche.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
